WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:37.640
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:37.910 --> 01:43.930
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.060 --> 01:46.810
[Episode 18]

4
02:12.360 --> 02:12.960
Well...

5
02:15.360 --> 02:16.680
I searched through more than a dozen train cars

6
02:16.680 --> 02:17.740
before I found you.

7
02:19.430 --> 02:20.870
W-Why are you...

8
02:21.150 --> 02:22.480
It's not because of you.

9
02:25.710 --> 02:27.310
It's not only because of you.

10
02:35.829 --> 02:36.640
Zhengliang!

11
02:42.910 --> 02:44.370
Have a drink before you go.

12
02:45.800 --> 02:47.460
I thought you'd already left.

13
02:48.079 --> 02:49.610
Why didn't you go to Guilin?

14
02:52.310 --> 02:53.520
I made all that up.

15
02:55.030 --> 02:55.810
I didn't hear back

16
02:55.810 --> 02:57.430
from a single hospital.

17
03:00.590 --> 03:01.910
I just don't get it.

18
03:01.960 --> 03:03.910
How did Chen ever fall for you?

19
03:05.190 --> 03:06.450
You're not just broke.

20
03:07.560 --> 03:08.470
You lie too.

21
03:09.430 --> 03:10.680
And on top of that,

22
03:11.840 --> 03:12.630
you're sick.

23
03:13.430 --> 03:14.710
Mentally.

24
03:15.330 --> 03:17.390
Physically, I'm perfectly healthy.

25
03:18.630 --> 03:19.310
Yeah.

26
03:23.870 --> 03:24.520
Fine.

27
03:25.360 --> 03:26.190
I'm sick.

28
03:31.370 --> 03:32.230
Can it kill you?

29
03:32.520 --> 03:33.310
What?

30
03:34.560 --> 03:36.820
I asked if your condition could kill you.

31
03:36.940 --> 03:38.160
In theory, no.

32
03:39.630 --> 03:41.170
In theory, no.

33
03:41.310 --> 03:42.840
Then what are you afraid of?

34
03:45.430 --> 03:46.490
I'm afraid of pain.

35
03:48.710 --> 03:49.630
Afraid of pain?

36
03:50.360 --> 03:52.560
All the more reason to go back with Chen.

37
03:53.079 --> 03:54.560
What heals pain

38
03:54.710 --> 03:55.520
better than

39
03:55.590 --> 03:56.910
family and friends?

40
03:58.760 --> 03:59.750
Well, you haven't told

41
03:59.750 --> 04:01.590
your mom you're sick either, have you?

42
04:01.590 --> 04:02.550
That's because I never

43
04:02.550 --> 04:05.190
got the chance to tell her, and now it's too late.

44
04:05.190 --> 04:06.000
Look.

45
04:09.750 --> 04:10.560
Chemotherapy

46
04:11.190 --> 04:12.080
can't save me.

47
04:13.000 --> 04:14.560
Neither can tears.

48
04:14.630 --> 04:16.160
I'm going to die either way.

49
04:17.750 --> 04:19.040
I'll face it alone.

50
04:19.310 --> 04:21.110
You can't go through this alone.

51
04:21.310 --> 04:22.840
When that day really comes,

52
04:24.430 --> 04:26.360
it'll only hurt your mom even more.

53
04:30.830 --> 04:31.630
Maybe.

54
04:33.870 --> 04:35.270
But I don't have a choice.

55
04:36.430 --> 04:37.390
Neither do I.

56
04:39.630 --> 04:40.730
Then let me share

57
04:40.750 --> 04:42.150
a theory of mine with you.

58
04:43.070 --> 04:43.960
Pain and memory

59
04:43.980 --> 04:45.270
cannot be separated.

60
04:45.510 --> 04:47.040
People can't simply

61
04:47.310 --> 04:49.270
choose to erase their memories.

62
04:49.800 --> 04:51.390
Even if you pretend to want to forget,

63
04:51.390 --> 04:52.720
the pain is still there.

64
04:54.120 --> 04:55.390
Simple example:

65
04:56.430 --> 04:58.290
this bottle of soy milk in my hand.

66
04:58.430 --> 04:59.560
If I put it down there

67
04:59.560 --> 05:00.430
on the ground,

68
05:00.750 --> 05:01.740
it looks like

69
05:01.760 --> 05:02.800
it's no longer in my hand.

70
05:02.800 --> 05:04.530
But it's still there, isn't it?

71
05:04.830 --> 05:05.630
Get it?

72
05:10.510 --> 05:11.310
Look.

73
05:12.510 --> 05:14.310
This is also a bottle of soy milk.

74
05:20.270 --> 05:20.920
Look,

75
05:21.630 --> 05:23.270
if you drink it, it's gone.

76
05:23.600 --> 05:25.190
Isn't it still in your stomach?

77
05:25.190 --> 05:26.510
Just wait for your body to digest it.

78
05:26.510 --> 05:28.120
Then it'll turn into urine, and you pee it out.

79
05:28.120 --> 05:29.490
It can't be digested.

80
05:30.560 --> 05:32.270
It's a figure of speech.

81
05:32.510 --> 05:33.360
"Metaphor."

82
05:33.630 --> 05:34.390
Get it?

83
05:35.000 --> 05:36.070
It's a metaphor.

84
05:36.159 --> 05:37.950
You can't put it into words.

85
05:38.070 --> 05:38.800
Just like...

86
06:03.650 --> 06:10.810
♪ It's only after something is lost that we begin to see ♪

87
06:06.000 --> 06:07.120
Okay, okay.

88
06:08.190 --> 06:09.000
You win.

89
06:09.920 --> 06:10.920
It's gone.

90
06:12.750 --> 06:18.440
♪ But some things can never be undone ♪

91
06:17.630 --> 06:18.390
Zhengliang.

92
06:20.480 --> 06:21.510
If you have nowhere to go,

93
06:21.460 --> 06:27.990
♪ When snowflakes cover all our yesterdays ♪

94
06:22.510 --> 06:23.430
just go home.

95
06:25.630 --> 06:26.630
As long as you're alive,

96
06:26.630 --> 06:27.960
you still have choices.

97
06:29.000 --> 06:30.240
At least you still have choices.

98
06:29.370 --> 06:35.260
♪ Perhaps it's best we leave the words unsaid ♪

99
06:36.360 --> 06:37.240
I'm sorry.

100
06:39.260 --> 06:46.480
♪ We were once someone else ♪

101
06:40.920 --> 06:42.000
I'm just saying.

102
06:43.830 --> 06:45.890
Whether you go home or not is up to you.

103
06:46.070 --> 06:47.530
No need to apologize to me.

104
06:48.090 --> 06:54.140
♪ Then, one day, we found our truest selves ♪

105
06:48.630 --> 06:49.890
I'm apologizing to you

106
06:51.270 --> 06:53.430
because I shouldn't have compared us like that.

107
06:53.430 --> 06:55.159
Our situations are different.

108
06:56.980 --> 07:03.910
♪ Turns out, you don't have to fall apart ♪

109
07:00.430 --> 07:01.240
Accepted.

110
07:04.630 --> 07:12.220
♪ To deserve a fresh start ♪

111
07:11.520 --> 07:14.890
[Dream Garden]

112
07:14.870 --> 07:21.620
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to erase the past ♪

113
07:23.640 --> 07:30.550
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

114
07:32.159 --> 07:35.150
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

115
07:32.560 --> 07:33.390
Zhengliang!

116
07:35.880 --> 07:39.670
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

117
07:36.510 --> 07:37.310
Bye-bye!

118
07:40.280 --> 07:48.390
♪ Maybe walking side by side for a while is enough ♪

119
07:51.720 --> 07:53.730
So you mean

120
07:54.510 --> 07:56.570
Pink Hair managed to talk you into it?

121
07:58.310 --> 07:59.260
The same words

122
07:59.280 --> 08:00.390
just hit differently

123
08:00.390 --> 08:02.050
coming from you than from him.

124
08:04.800 --> 08:05.620
Actually, deep down,

125
08:05.620 --> 08:07.070
I was still wavering

126
08:08.110 --> 08:09.750
until I saw someone.

127
08:24.510 --> 08:27.240
Son, Happy New Year.

128
08:32.870 --> 08:34.150
Son, look.

129
08:36.150 --> 08:37.409
Those migratory birds

130
08:38.720 --> 08:40.480
fly south for the winter,

131
08:41.320 --> 08:42.600
but when spring comes,

132
08:43.080 --> 08:44.210
they always return.

133
08:47.630 --> 08:49.550
They know where they want to go.

134
09:02.440 --> 09:03.440
Happy New Year.

135
09:05.720 --> 09:06.550
I think

136
09:07.200 --> 09:09.150
that might mean I've taken

137
09:09.670 --> 09:11.270
a step forward emotionally.

138
09:11.870 --> 09:13.020
And after everything that's happened,

139
09:13.020 --> 09:14.960
I guess it was also the result of...

140
09:15.790 --> 09:17.600
of a combination of factors.

141
09:18.550 --> 09:20.880
I didn't understand a single word of that,

142
09:21.270 --> 09:22.320
but I like how you

143
09:22.340 --> 09:23.860
act all profound.

144
09:24.080 --> 09:25.200
I'm not acting...

145
09:25.200 --> 09:25.960
Okay.

146
09:26.720 --> 09:27.960
Profound without even realizing it.

147
09:27.960 --> 09:28.670
Happy now?

148
09:31.750 --> 09:34.360
Actually, my mom and your mom were very close.

149
09:35.480 --> 09:36.770
But I don't know much about her.

150
09:36.770 --> 09:38.300
What kind of person was she?

151
09:44.390 --> 09:45.240
My mom was...

152
09:45.750 --> 09:47.150
was a really good person.

153
09:47.630 --> 09:48.670
That's for sure.

154
09:50.750 --> 09:51.550
What else?

155
09:53.670 --> 09:54.720
Well...

156
09:56.960 --> 09:57.870
When she was young,

157
09:57.870 --> 09:59.730
she worked at a beverage factory.

158
10:03.790 --> 10:05.360
A-And then...

159
10:06.600 --> 10:08.480
she seemed to have taught herself...

160
10:08.480 --> 10:10.880
taught herself accounting a few years ago.

161
10:13.390 --> 10:14.200
Go on.

162
10:15.200 --> 10:16.510
And then she...

163
10:26.720 --> 10:28.250
Now that you're going back,

164
10:28.360 --> 10:30.160
are you still planning to leave?

165
10:35.440 --> 10:36.480
You...

166
10:37.030 --> 10:37.890
I-I-If...

167
10:38.480 --> 10:39.350
If you haven't made up your mind,

168
10:39.350 --> 10:39.960
get off the train and think about it.

169
10:39.960 --> 10:40.670
No.

170
10:41.000 --> 10:42.000
I have to see if I can

171
10:42.000 --> 10:43.930
make it through this winter first.

172
11:03.840 --> 11:04.630
Jia Xin!

173
11:06.480 --> 11:07.240
Jia Xin!

174
11:17.910 --> 11:19.030
What are you doing here?

175
11:19.030 --> 11:19.840
Missed me?

176
11:26.270 --> 11:27.390
Aren't you short of money?

177
11:27.390 --> 11:28.080
Here.

178
11:31.390 --> 11:32.150
Where did you get it?

179
11:32.150 --> 11:33.670
Don't worry about that.

180
11:34.030 --> 11:35.360
Remember to pay me back.

181
11:36.790 --> 11:37.850
Here's your money.

182
11:38.790 --> 11:40.390
I've already borrowed some.

183
11:41.270 --> 11:42.030
Really?

184
11:42.030 --> 11:43.200
Who did you borrow it from?

185
11:43.200 --> 11:43.960
Gong Xue.

186
11:44.150 --> 11:45.410
She lent me 2,000 yuan.

187
11:47.200 --> 11:48.200
Gong Xue?

188
11:48.750 --> 11:50.410
How do you two know each other?

189
11:50.440 --> 11:51.840
Did you lose your memory?

190
11:52.150 --> 11:52.960
Didn't you introduce us

191
11:52.960 --> 11:54.620
when I came to your workplace?

192
11:56.240 --> 11:56.960
Wait.

193
11:57.510 --> 11:58.720
You two didn't even speak that day.

194
11:58.720 --> 11:59.720
How did you get close enough

195
11:59.720 --> 12:00.510
for her to lend you money?

196
12:00.510 --> 12:00.910
Well,

197
12:01.030 --> 12:02.320
we were talking by the entrance that day,

198
12:02.320 --> 12:03.360
and she overheard us.

199
12:03.360 --> 12:04.820
Then she lent me the money.

200
12:06.720 --> 12:07.670
Take my 2,000

201
12:07.670 --> 12:09.080
and pay her back.

202
12:09.360 --> 12:09.720
Pay her back.

203
12:09.720 --> 12:10.910
W-What?

204
12:11.080 --> 12:11.840
No.

205
12:13.550 --> 12:15.750
Ever heard of "borrow nine, repay thirteen"?

206
12:15.750 --> 12:17.210
I borrowed 2,000 from her,

207
12:17.440 --> 12:19.960
and I have to pay her back

208
12:20.150 --> 12:21.080
2,888.88 yuan.

209
12:21.390 --> 12:22.390
Not a cent less.

210
12:34.740 --> 12:35.730
[Gong's Blind Massage]

211
12:39.550 --> 12:40.310
Zhengguang,

212
12:40.340 --> 12:42.580
a-aren't you off today?

213
12:51.150 --> 12:51.960
Gong Xue.

214
12:51.920 --> 12:55.020
[Healing Hands]

215
12:52.440 --> 12:54.240
Why did you lend money to Jia Xin?

216
12:55.020 --> 12:56.420
[Traditional Chinese Health Therapy; Dispel Dampness, Boost Qi]

217
12:55.390 --> 12:56.480
Shouldn't I have?

218
12:56.540 --> 12:59.000
[Blind Massage; Relieve Tension & Improve Circulation]

219
12:57.000 --> 12:58.120
Lending is fine,

220
12:58.120 --> 12:59.960
but you can't charge him loan-shark interest.

221
12:59.960 --> 13:02.960
What's all this "borrow nine, repay thirteen" stuff?

222
13:03.200 --> 13:04.870
I need to make money too.

223
13:05.240 --> 13:06.270
Besides,

224
13:06.360 --> 13:07.960
we already agreed on the terms.

225
13:07.960 --> 13:09.290
Why are you sticking your nose into this?

226
13:09.290 --> 13:18.560
[Therapeutic Massage; Daily Care, Pain Relief]

227
13:11.550 --> 13:13.000
You two met through me,

228
13:13.000 --> 13:13.670
right?

229
13:14.670 --> 13:15.480
So what?

230
13:16.030 --> 13:17.270
Don't come to me if something goes wrong.

231
13:17.270 --> 13:18.480
It's fine.

232
13:18.630 --> 13:19.910
I've already lent him the money.

233
13:19.910 --> 13:21.910
Worst case, he goes back on his word.

234
13:22.720 --> 13:25.000
But I believe he won't.

235
13:25.960 --> 13:26.840
Why do you believe

236
13:26.840 --> 13:27.390
he won't?

237
13:28.320 --> 13:30.390
Because he has a nice voice.

238
13:31.390 --> 13:32.910
Voices don't lie.

239
13:48.670 --> 13:50.530
What are you really trying to ask?

240
13:54.030 --> 13:54.840
I...

241
14:01.630 --> 14:03.560
Your heart is beating really fast.

242
14:04.080 --> 14:05.340
You seem very nervous.

243
14:07.630 --> 14:08.480
I'm not.

244
14:09.530 --> 14:13.010
[Therapeutic Massage; Daily Care, Pain Relief]

245
14:14.080 --> 14:15.140
What are you doing?

246
14:16.890 --> 14:20.220
[Traditional Chinese Health Therapy; Dispel Dampness, Boost Qi]

247
14:17.840 --> 14:20.040
Which one of you is massaging me anyway?

248
14:20.600 --> 14:21.360
Mr. Wu?

249
14:23.000 --> 14:24.130
You know each other?

250
14:24.550 --> 14:26.030
Perfect. Then this client's yours.

251
14:26.030 --> 14:26.870
Get to work.

252
14:27.870 --> 14:28.670
Wait...

253
14:33.870 --> 14:35.080
You like Xue?

254
14:37.790 --> 14:39.270
No, don't talk nonsense.

255
14:40.030 --> 14:40.840
That's good.

256
14:41.030 --> 14:42.960
I don't think she likes you anyway.

257
14:43.320 --> 14:44.650
Are you any good at this?

258
14:46.240 --> 14:48.040
Don't go pressing random spots.

259
14:51.360 --> 14:52.120
Zhengguang,

260
14:52.750 --> 14:54.480
you were really rough with that massage.

261
14:54.480 --> 14:55.150
Why do I get the feeling

262
14:55.150 --> 14:56.720
you're using this chance to get back at me?

263
14:56.720 --> 14:57.480
No.

264
14:58.630 --> 14:59.270
Alright.

265
14:59.510 --> 15:00.510
Take care, Mr. Wu.

266
15:07.440 --> 15:08.240
Zhengguang.

267
15:09.630 --> 15:11.600
I know Gong Yi and his daughter

268
15:11.600 --> 15:12.240
quite well.

269
15:12.240 --> 15:14.370
We've known each other for a long time.

270
15:14.910 --> 15:15.720
Their family's eyes

271
15:15.720 --> 15:17.920
really do light up at the sight of money.

272
15:18.670 --> 15:21.200
-Mr. Wu, I think sometimes you... -Calm down.

273
15:21.910 --> 15:24.110
Doesn't medical treatment cost money?

274
15:24.600 --> 15:26.550
When I say that,

275
15:28.720 --> 15:30.480
I mean it literally.

276
15:46.630 --> 15:47.300
[Exit] [Entrance] [Tickets]

277
15:50.120 --> 15:51.250
Where are you going?

278
15:51.390 --> 15:53.390
I'm going back to my parents' place.

279
15:53.550 --> 15:54.410
What about you?

280
15:54.670 --> 15:55.530
I'm going home.

281
15:56.270 --> 15:57.730
How are you getting there?

282
15:57.790 --> 15:58.720
I'll take a taxi.

283
15:59.150 --> 15:59.840
And you?

284
16:01.030 --> 16:03.030
I suddenly feel like taking the bus.

285
16:03.870 --> 16:05.240
Well, I'm off that way, then.

286
16:05.240 --> 16:05.960
Bye-bye.

287
16:08.580 --> 16:11.330
[Bus]

288
16:22.550 --> 16:23.990
Why are you back?

289
16:24.010 --> 16:25.810
Weren't you going to take a taxi?

290
16:29.480 --> 16:31.680
I suddenly feel like taking the bus too.

291
16:33.720 --> 16:34.520
Let's go then.

292
16:55.240 --> 16:56.570
What are you staring at?

293
16:58.080 --> 16:59.120
Nothing.

294
17:01.270 --> 17:02.550
I was just thinking...

295
17:04.589 --> 17:06.990
This doesn't seem like something you'd do.

296
17:07.640 --> 17:10.240
How come you're willing to take the bus with me?

297
17:13.109 --> 17:14.770
My rational side tells me that

298
17:15.000 --> 17:16.400
since I've made up my mind

299
17:16.400 --> 17:17.349
to come back,

300
17:17.589 --> 17:19.720
I have to... have to make some changes.

301
17:20.880 --> 17:21.680
Like what?

302
17:23.589 --> 17:24.400
Like...

303
17:26.030 --> 17:26.960
working hard,

304
17:27.240 --> 17:28.040
saving money,

305
17:28.920 --> 17:29.640
and improving my relationships

306
17:29.640 --> 17:31.100
with the people around me.

307
17:31.880 --> 17:32.680
And, well...

308
17:32.790 --> 17:35.270
B-Being a bit nicer to Liu Zhengguang.

309
17:38.720 --> 17:39.510
That's it?

310
17:43.160 --> 17:44.360
Nothing else like...

311
17:45.200 --> 17:47.000
Like your relationship with me?

312
17:49.680 --> 17:50.070
Well,

313
17:50.070 --> 17:51.330
didn't I just say that?

314
17:51.640 --> 17:53.030
I'll be nicer

315
17:53.030 --> 17:54.680
to everyone around me.

316
17:55.160 --> 17:56.160
Not just you.

317
17:58.110 --> 18:00.510
I-I don't see what this has to do with me.

318
18:01.920 --> 18:03.530
It does. Aren't you...

319
18:03.590 --> 18:04.880
Aren't you one of the people around me?

320
18:04.880 --> 18:05.920
You're included.

321
18:06.200 --> 18:08.070
I'm just not singling you out.

322
18:15.590 --> 18:16.350
Actually, from...

323
18:16.350 --> 18:17.880
from the bottom of my heart,

324
18:18.270 --> 18:19.880
I'm grateful to you for...

325
18:20.270 --> 18:21.440
for what you...

326
18:21.440 --> 18:22.240
Shut up.

327
18:40.070 --> 18:40.720
Thank you.

328
18:40.760 --> 18:47.780
[1314 Funeral Services]

329
18:46.070 --> 18:47.310
Why are you trying to

330
18:47.310 --> 18:48.110
build that?

331
18:49.350 --> 18:51.070
We don't need more shelves.

332
18:51.680 --> 18:53.310
It's not for goods.

333
18:58.550 --> 18:59.510
Then what is it for?

334
18:59.510 --> 19:00.270
I want to

335
19:00.290 --> 19:02.090
take all those things you stole—

336
19:02.350 --> 19:04.720
your little trophies—

337
19:05.240 --> 19:07.240
and put them all on this shelf.

338
19:07.240 --> 19:08.690
Didn't you tell me to

339
19:08.710 --> 19:09.680
throw all those things away?

340
19:09.680 --> 19:10.790
I was thinking,

341
19:11.510 --> 19:12.590
if we put them here,

342
19:12.790 --> 19:15.050
you could look at them whenever you want.

343
19:15.110 --> 19:17.240
And every time you look at them,

344
19:17.240 --> 19:18.000
you'd feel

345
19:18.000 --> 19:19.400
a sense of satisfaction.

346
19:20.270 --> 19:21.240
Then maybe you wouldn't feel the urge

347
19:21.240 --> 19:22.480
to steal anymore.

348
19:24.160 --> 19:25.880
Well, you've got that wrong.

349
19:29.240 --> 19:31.160
A shelf this pretty will make me

350
19:33.030 --> 19:34.270
want to steal

351
19:34.270 --> 19:35.310
even more.

352
19:40.310 --> 19:41.110
Amy.

353
19:42.880 --> 19:43.750
I...

354
19:45.400 --> 19:47.600
don't want to be apart from you anymore.

355
19:49.270 --> 19:50.270
Not even for a day.

356
19:52.750 --> 19:54.720
San...

357
19:55.510 --> 19:58.480
Then I'll just be more careful when I steal.

358
19:59.110 --> 20:00.240
I'm back!

359
20:00.960 --> 20:02.020
What are you doing?

360
20:04.350 --> 20:05.680
Being all lovey-dovey out in the open

361
20:05.680 --> 20:07.410
without even trying to hide it?

362
20:08.440 --> 20:09.550
Y-You're back.

363
20:10.680 --> 20:12.140
Nothing happened, right?

364
20:12.400 --> 20:13.200
Look.

365
20:13.510 --> 20:14.910
I got back safe and sound.

366
20:15.400 --> 20:16.110
What are you looking at?

367
20:16.110 --> 20:17.680
You look so happy.

368
20:18.240 --> 20:19.480
You must have brought

369
20:19.480 --> 20:20.940
that "Potato Chips" back.

370
20:21.070 --> 20:21.790
Where is he?

371
20:23.680 --> 20:24.350
No.

372
20:24.550 --> 20:25.880
I didn't bring him back.

373
20:26.200 --> 20:27.330
He didn't come back?

374
20:27.640 --> 20:28.510
No.

375
20:28.880 --> 20:30.510
Then did he come back or not?

376
20:30.920 --> 20:32.400
H-He's back.

377
20:32.510 --> 20:33.310
Where is he?

378
20:34.680 --> 20:36.080
He went back to his house.

379
20:40.480 --> 20:42.000
He came back with you.

380
20:42.400 --> 20:44.600
So have the two of you made any progress?

381
20:45.830 --> 20:46.440
Yes.

382
20:46.480 --> 20:48.110
But... But not much.

383
20:48.350 --> 20:49.750
"Not much"?

384
20:50.270 --> 20:51.050
You traveled

385
20:51.080 --> 20:53.480
thousands of miles all by yourself for him.

386
20:54.030 --> 20:55.400
You didn't beat him up, did you?

387
20:55.400 --> 20:56.590
You... You...

388
20:56.720 --> 20:58.250
What are you talking about?

389
20:58.640 --> 21:00.100
You two don't understand.

390
21:00.270 --> 21:01.640
I'm so gentle.

391
21:03.110 --> 21:04.400
I'm gonna go change.

392
21:05.550 --> 21:07.110
Why are you looking at me?

393
21:07.510 --> 21:09.570
I'm looking to see if you understand.

394
21:15.510 --> 21:17.310
Zhengguang, I'm back.

395
21:20.510 --> 21:21.310
Brother.

396
21:21.590 --> 21:23.640
Although we've only been apart for a few days,

397
21:23.640 --> 21:25.500
I've missed you so much, Brother.

398
21:31.070 --> 21:31.880
Who are you?

399
21:32.400 --> 21:33.680
I'm your brother, Liu Zhengliang.

400
21:33.680 --> 21:34.680
Who else could I be?

401
21:34.680 --> 21:35.590
No way.

402
21:35.750 --> 21:36.830
Liu Zhengliang would never

403
21:36.830 --> 21:37.720
say something like that.

404
21:37.720 --> 21:38.790
I'm calling the police.

405
21:38.790 --> 21:39.960
Are you serious?

406
21:40.590 --> 21:41.850
You're overreacting.

407
21:43.160 --> 21:43.960
Move aside.

408
21:48.350 --> 21:49.680
Didn't you go to Fuzhou?

409
21:49.680 --> 21:50.750
Why are you back?

410
21:52.400 --> 21:53.550
Some things came up.

411
21:53.830 --> 21:55.070
It's a long story.

412
21:56.350 --> 21:57.440
You can't just do this.

413
21:57.440 --> 21:59.240
Didn't I tell you to let me know in advance?

414
21:59.240 --> 22:00.240
You gave me no time to

415
22:00.240 --> 22:00.680
mentally prepare for this.

416
22:00.680 --> 22:02.210
What are you talking about?

417
22:02.550 --> 22:03.550
I'm just coming home.

418
22:03.550 --> 22:05.550
What kind of mental preparation...

419
22:09.640 --> 22:10.310
Yes.

420
22:10.920 --> 22:12.250
You're right, Brother.

421
22:12.550 --> 22:13.750
It's all my fault.

422
22:14.070 --> 22:14.870
Tell you what.

423
22:15.070 --> 22:16.590
Next time I come back,

424
22:16.640 --> 22:18.040
I'll tell you in advance.

425
22:22.920 --> 22:24.590
Then how long are you staying?

426
22:26.480 --> 22:27.940
Anywhere from a few months

427
22:28.160 --> 22:29.440
to the rest of my life.

428
22:32.070 --> 22:33.310
Do you really mean it?

429
22:39.310 --> 22:40.110
Zhengguang,

430
22:40.960 --> 22:41.920
you're the only family

431
22:41.920 --> 22:43.050
I have in this world.

432
22:43.790 --> 22:45.190
We have to stay together.

433
22:50.310 --> 22:51.480
Why does it sound so gross

434
22:51.480 --> 22:52.550
coming out of your mouth?

435
22:52.550 --> 22:53.480
From now on,

436
22:54.160 --> 22:54.920
I'll fulfill my duty

437
22:54.920 --> 22:56.120
as your older brother

438
22:56.590 --> 22:57.990
and take good care of you.

439
23:06.000 --> 23:06.800
What's wrong?

440
23:07.550 --> 23:08.510
What happened?

441
23:09.310 --> 23:10.710
What could've happened?

442
23:11.880 --> 23:12.680
Well?

443
23:12.960 --> 23:14.110
Are you moved by how much

444
23:14.110 --> 23:15.000
I've changed?

445
23:15.720 --> 23:16.440
I...

446
23:16.440 --> 23:17.880
I don't dare to move.

447
23:18.350 --> 23:19.160
I feel like you're

448
23:19.160 --> 23:20.200
a monster in disguise.

449
23:20.200 --> 23:21.480
If I make a move, you'll eat me.

450
23:21.480 --> 23:23.210
You're being way too dramatic.

451
23:24.960 --> 23:25.920
I-I'm a little overwhelmed.

452
23:25.920 --> 23:27.200
My brain can't...

453
23:27.440 --> 23:29.440
It's all too much. I need some time to process this.

454
23:29.440 --> 23:30.400
I'm off to work.

455
23:31.400 --> 23:32.200
Brother.

456
23:32.830 --> 23:33.960
You found a new job?

457
23:34.240 --> 23:35.900
Congratulations. Come here.

458
23:40.550 --> 23:41.270
Don't move.

459
23:42.790 --> 23:43.720
Don't come over.

460
23:45.200 --> 23:46.200
I'm going to work.

461
23:49.400 --> 23:50.550
Seriously?

462
23:52.480 --> 23:53.270
Take it easy.

463
23:53.590 --> 23:55.590
Zhengguang, be careful on the road!

464
24:10.400 --> 24:11.730
I'm being a bit too much.

465
24:22.270 --> 24:23.200
All these years,

466
24:23.550 --> 24:25.030
I seem to have been thinking

467
24:25.030 --> 24:26.480
only about how to get away from here—

468
24:26.480 --> 24:27.440
the further

469
24:27.550 --> 24:28.640
the better.

470
24:29.640 --> 24:30.160
But when I really found myself

471
24:30.160 --> 24:32.220
with absolutely nothing, I realized

472
24:32.720 --> 24:34.310
how good it feels to be home.

473
24:35.160 --> 24:36.960
Being with family

474
24:37.960 --> 24:38.760
feels so good.

475
24:47.040 --> 24:50.500
[Police]

476
25:08.380 --> 25:09.400
[Police]

477
25:10.430 --> 25:10.830
[Court]

478
25:10.860 --> 25:12.840
[Police]

479
25:24.220 --> 25:26.460
[Police]

